<span id="S1.T1.6.1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">The diagram shows <span id="S1.T1.6.1.2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#006400;">two intersecting circles</span>, … , an external <span id="S1.T1.6.1.2.3.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">point <math id="S1.T1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math></span> lies still farther to the right, … <span id="S1.T1.6.1.2.3.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#006400;">red chords</span> <math id="S1.T1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\!N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.639em;" width="0.639em"><mi>B</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\!N</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.T1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J\!Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.481em;" width="0.481em"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">J</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J\!Z</annotation></semantics></math>, …</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S1.T1.6.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
